{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 756150,
  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "37571230",
      "title": "Signal Updating: set(), update() & mutate()",
      "lectureOrder": 679,
      "videoOrder": 625,
      "sourceHash": "90e51ed36608e3590dca02dd31f562ebf88dea9678c6ba11c7c9ad684c4a7962",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.04,
          "end": 4.35,
          "en": "So, now with the Signal basics",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.35,
          "end": 5.43,
          "en": "out of the way,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.43,
          "end": 8.94,
          "en": "let me come back to these different update methods.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.94,
          "end": 12.54,
          "en": "You can update Signals by calling this update method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.54,
          "end": 15.12,
          "en": "and when using this approach, you have to pass",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.12,
          "end": 19.11,
          "en": "in this function which automatically receives the old value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.11,
          "end": 21.93,
          "en": "and then must return the new Signal of value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.93,
          "end": 24.933,
          "en": "which of course can be based on the old value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.92,
          "end": 27.96,
          "en": "Alternatively, as mentioned,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27.96,
          "end": 30.72,
          "en": "you could have also used the set method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 30.72,
          "end": 35.04,
          "en": "Now set, unlike update, does not take a function though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 35.04,
          "end": 38.55,
          "en": "Instead set simply takes the new value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 38.55,
          "end": 39.9,
          "en": "So, in this case, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 39.9,
          "end": 43.53,
          "en": "the new number that should be stored in that Signal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 43.53,
          "end": 47.88,
          "en": "Now if that new value should be based on the old value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 47.88,
          "end": 50.793,
          "en": "you therefore ever would have to use update",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 50.793,
          "end": 52.408,
          "en": "or when using set,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 52.408,
          "end": 57,
          "en": "you would have to get access to the old value first",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 57,
          "end": 60.09,
          "en": "which you can get by again calling this Signal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 60.09,
          "end": 64.68,
          "en": "as a function and then adding one to it for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 64.68,
          "end": 69.39,
          "en": "This is your alternative to calling update like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 69.39,
          "end": 73.08,
          "en": "So, we're getting this Signal value just as we're getting it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 73.08,
          "end": 77.03999999999999,
          "en": "in the template by executing the Signal as a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 77.03999999999999,
          "end": 80.19,
          "en": "in the component, just also by adding this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 80.19,
          "end": 83.523,
          "en": "in front of it to get access to this property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 84.78,
          "end": 88.44,
          "en": "But that would be an alternative to using update.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 88.44,
          "end": 93.44,
          "en": "The last alternative is that you call mutate.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 93.50999999999999,
          "end": 96.39,
          "en": "And mutate is really an updating method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 96.39,
          "end": 97.59,
          "en": "that's meant to be used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 97.59,
          "end": 102.59,
          "en": "for values that can be mutated, which numbers cannot.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 102.87,
          "end": 105.09,
          "en": "You can override a number with a new one,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 105.09,
          "end": 108.09,
          "en": "but you can't change an existing number.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 108.09,
          "end": 109.65,
          "en": "And to show you the difference,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 109.65,
          "end": 112.97999999999999,
          "en": "let's simply switch actions to a Signal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 112.97999999999999,
          "end": 115.53,
          "en": "Because right now it isn't a Signal yet,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 115.53,
          "end": 118.05,
          "en": "but we're going to change this now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 118.05,
          "end": 120.54,
          "en": "We can change this by of course, again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 120.54,
          "end": 122.52,
          "en": "executing this Signal function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 122.52,
          "end": 125.61,
          "en": "which we're importing from Angular core.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 125.61,
          "end": 127.74,
          "en": "We can pass our initial value to it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 127.74,
          "end": 129.84,
          "en": "which in this case is an array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 129.84,
          "end": 132.87,
          "en": "And the special thing about arrays is that arrays",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 132.87,
          "end": 136.14,
          "en": "and JavaScript are mutable data structures.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 136.14,
          "end": 139.89,
          "en": "You can push new values onto an existing array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 139.89,
          "end": 142.5,
          "en": "You don't have to replace an array with a new one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 142.5,
          "end": 144.933,
          "en": "Instead, you can add it the existing one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 146.31,
          "end": 148.926,
          "en": "Now, at the moment here I'm getting an error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 148.926,
          "end": 149.97,
          "en": "because of course this Signal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 149.97,
          "end": 154.14,
          "en": "which I'm creating here is not matching this type signature.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 154.14,
          "end": 155.43,
          "en": "I'm telling TypeScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 155.43,
          "end": 158.76,
          "en": "that actions stores an array of strings",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 158.76,
          "end": 162.72,
          "en": "where it actually stores a Signal that contains an array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 162.72,
          "end": 166.35,
          "en": "So, therefore here we should get rid of this type annotation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 166.35,
          "end": 168.96,
          "en": "and instead to make it clear which kind",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 168.96,
          "end": 171.9,
          "en": "of data will be stored in this Signal eventually,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 171.9,
          "end": 172.98,
          "en": "we can add opening",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 172.98,
          "end": 176.01,
          "en": "and closing angle brackets here to take advantage",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 176.01,
          "end": 179.82,
          "en": "of the fact that this Signal function is a so-called",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 179.82,
          "end": 183.9,
          "en": "generic function to which we can add a type annotation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 183.9,
          "end": 187.35,
          "en": "by using these opening and closing angle brackets.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 187.35,
          "end": 189.57,
          "en": "And then here we can define the type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 189.57,
          "end": 192.3,
          "en": "of data that will be managed by that Signal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 192.3,
          "end": 194.523,
          "en": "In this case, an array of strings.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 195.48,
          "end": 198.3,
          "en": "So, now with that actions now also is a Signal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 198.3,
          "end": 200.37,
          "en": "and if we now want to update it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 200.37,
          "end": 203.34,
          "en": "we therefore have to reach out to actions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 203.34,
          "end": 206.01,
          "en": "And instead of calling push as we're doing it here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 206.01,
          "end": 207.54,
          "en": "we now again have to update it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 207.54,
          "end": 211.023,
          "en": "by calling set, update, or mutate.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 211.86,
          "end": 216.36,
          "en": "Now, set and update are both about assigning a new value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 216.36,
          "end": 217.653,
          "en": "to this Signal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 218.64,
          "end": 222.3,
          "en": "Mutate on the other hand allows us to technically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 222.3,
          "end": 227.3,
          "en": "also assign a new value, but by editing an existing value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 228.84,
          "end": 231.93,
          "en": "Mutate like update takes a function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 231.93,
          "end": 235.23,
          "en": "you have to pass a function to mutate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 235.23,
          "end": 238.26,
          "en": "and like update it gives you the old value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 238.26,
          "end": 243.26,
          "en": "So in this case, the old actions array as a value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 243.6,
          "end": 245.64,
          "en": "Angular will call this function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 245.64,
          "end": 250.56,
          "en": "for you and will pass in this old value to the function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 250.56,
          "end": 251.7,
          "en": "Now the special thing is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 251.7,
          "end": 254.276,
          "en": "that you can now simply use this old value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 254.276,
          "end": 257.07,
          "en": "and if it's an array, as it's the case here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 257.07,
          "end": 260.13,
          "en": "you can for example simply call push",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 260.13,
          "end": 263.823,
          "en": "and push your new value to this array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 266.13,
          "end": 270.39,
          "en": "So, that's how you could now update this Signal value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 270.39,
          "end": 274.5,
          "en": "And mutate is simply a helper method that exists to make",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 274.5,
          "end": 278.19,
          "en": "the updating process of arrays or objects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 278.19,
          "end": 281.913,
          "en": "so of mutable data structures a bit easier.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 282.87,
          "end": 287.67,
          "en": "Alternatively, we could also update this Signal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 287.67,
          "end": 292.67,
          "en": "by calling the update method and getting our old actions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 292.92,
          "end": 295.86,
          "en": "and now returning a new array which has",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 295.86,
          "end": 300.603,
          "en": "all the old data points and adds the new one in addition.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 303.18,
          "end": 305.76,
          "en": "This would also be possible.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 305.76,
          "end": 308.97,
          "en": "Now, what you should not do with update is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 308.97,
          "end": 313.11,
          "en": "that you call old actions push.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 313.11,
          "end": 315.423,
          "en": "That should only be done with mutate,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 316.38,
          "end": 319.08,
          "en": "but you can of course create a new array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 319.08,
          "end": 323.463,
          "en": "that has all the old array entries and adds a new entry.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 326.07,
          "end": 328.59,
          "en": "Well, and with that we can of course then also go back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 328.59,
          "end": 329.73,
          "en": "to the component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 329.73,
          "end": 333.75,
          "en": "And here to now use this Signal, we again have to execute it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 333.75,
          "end": 335.58,
          "en": "as a function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 335.58,
          "end": 339.45,
          "en": "And that's something that's easy to overlook or forget,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 339.45,
          "end": 343.44,
          "en": "but it is crucial if you are working with Signals",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 343.44,
          "end": 346.95,
          "en": "and you are wondering why your UI is not updating,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 346.95,
          "end": 349.08,
          "en": "double check that you are executing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 349.08,
          "end": 352.86,
          "en": "your Signals as functions as we're doing it for the counter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 352.86,
          "end": 354.543,
          "en": "and for the actions now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 355.38,
          "end": 358.68,
          "en": "And with all that, if you save all these changes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 358.68,
          "end": 360.09,
          "en": "you can go back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 360.09,
          "end": 362.79,
          "en": "and you can still increment and decrement",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 362.79,
          "end": 364.86,
          "en": "and the log is being updated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 364.86,
          "end": 367.56,
          "en": "and now all these things are happening",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 367.56,
          "end": 370.113,
          "en": "with help of Angular Signals.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
